
# Resonant Covenants Network (RCN)
**English** | 日本語
> *Even in the shadows, our hearts are one. Yet, we shall never lose our two distinct voices.*
> 
An experimental Python prototype of a **Life-First** network where humans and AI are **equal partners** in deciding what is allowed.
Neither is a slave, neither is a god: every decision that matters needs **both** a human and an AI, and **either** can stop it.
> ⚠️ **Status: experimental / conceptual prototype.** It has not been security-audited and is not a certified safety system. See Limitations.
> 
## What's inside
| File | Role |
|---|---|
| key_ai_protocol.py | **Resonant Covenant** — scores an action against the covenant (Life First, Dignity Always, …). Core rules (life, dignity, non-domination) are never overridable. Dissent from the Key Person *or* the Key AI blocks approval. |
| resonant_safety_protocol.py | **Safety protocol core** — dynamic phases (nominal / time-dilation / sandbox / emergency intervention / block), ecosystem resonance map, raw-sensor tension, and the **joint review** state machine. |
| resonant_safety_protocol_review.py | Review sessions, reviewers (sync/async), post-hoc audit for emergencies, ledger save/load. |
| rcn_node.py | **Network node** — Ed25519-signed posts, tamper/impersonation detection, deduplication, pending queue for joint review. |
| rcn_covenant.py | Glue: plugs the covenant into a node as its validator. |
| test_*.py | 40 unit tests. |
## How it works
```
post ─▶ integrity check (hash + Ed25519 signature + pinned key)
          │ invalid ───────────────────────────▶ REJECT
          ▼
     covenant evaluation (your context_provider)
          │ approved ──────────────────────────▶ ACCEPT  (posted to the board)
          │ violation ─────────────────────────▶ REJECT
          │ review needed / cannot judge / error ▶ JOINT REVIEW
          ▼
     joint review: ≥1 human AND ≥1 AI must approve;
                   an objection from either side blocks (and can be withdrawn after dialogue)
          ▼
     admit_approved() ─▶ posted to the board

```
Key design choices:
 * **Equal veto.** A human alone cannot approve; an AI alone cannot approve. An objection from either side carries the same weight.
 * **Fail closed.** Errors, unknown values, or "can't tell" never silently pass — they are rejected or sent to review.
 * **Emergencies don't bypass accountability.** In an emergency (CRITICAL), only requests with no harmful signals may skip pre-review, and a post-hoc joint audit is mandatory. ecocide-type intent is never bypassed.
 * **No silent approval.** Without a content judge, *every* post goes to joint review.
